msgid "signin.nearby.title"
msgstr "Approve on your other device"

#. Sign in with your phone
#. Nearby sign-in, before the system asks for access to the local network.
msgid "signin.nearby.promptTitle"
msgstr "Sign in with your phone"

#. Open {app} on a phone or computer that's signed in and on this network.
#. Nearby sign-in, waiting. Arguments: {app} = the app's name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.body"
msgstr "Open {app} on a phone or computer that's signed in and on this network."

#. Tap this code there:
#. Nearby sign-in, waiting: the line above the code the other device must tap.
msgid "signin.nearby.match"
msgstr "Tap this code there:"

#. Use a code instead
#. Nearby sign-in, waiting: switches to the device code.
msgid "signin.nearby.code"
msgstr "Use a code instead"

#. macos: Use a Code Instead
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "signin.nearby.code"
msgstr "Use a Code Instead"

#. Signed in as {email}
#. Nearby sign-in, done. Arguments: {email} = the account's email address (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.done"
msgstr "Signed in as {email}"

#. Not you?
#. Nearby sign-in, done: opens the sign-out and review step when the account is not the person's.
msgid "signin.nearby.notYou"
msgstr "Not you?"

#. macos: Not You?
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "signin.nearby.notYou"
msgstr "Not You?"

#. Next, allow {app} to find devices on your network, so your phone can sign you in.
#. Nearby sign-in: shown before the system asks for access to devices on the local network (L-11). Arguments: {app} = the app's name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.prePrompt"
msgstr "Next, allow {app} to find devices on your network, so your phone can sign you in."

#. Let {device} sign in?
#. Nearby approval, on the signed-in device. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.ask"
msgstr "Let {device} sign in?"

#. Tap the code it shows.
#. Nearby approval: number matching. Three 6-digit codes follow; one matches the code the new device shows. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.askBody"
msgstr "Tap the code it shows."

#. {device} is signed in
#. Nearby approval: the new device is signed in. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.approved"
msgstr "{device} is signed in"

#. {device} isn't on this network
#. Nearby approval: the new device is not on the approver's network. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.notNearby"
msgstr "{device} isn't on this network"

#. Connect both to the same Wi-Fi, or sign in with a code on {device}.
#. Nearby approval: the new device is not on the approver's network. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.notNearbyBody"
msgstr "Connect both to the same Wi-Fi, or sign in with a code on {device}."

#. That code didn't match, so {device} wasn't signed in.
#. Nearby approval: the person tapped a code that did not match; the request is denied. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.mismatch"
msgstr "That code didn't match, so {device} wasn't signed in."

#. Approve a nearby device
#. Account menu entry: opens the nearby approval list on the signed-in device.
msgid "signin.nearby.menu"
msgstr "Approve a nearby device"

#. macos: Approve a Nearby Device
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "signin.nearby.menu"
msgstr "Approve a Nearby Device"

#. Choose a license for {device}
#. Nearby approval, on the signed-in device: choose which license the new device gets. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.chooseTitle"
msgstr "Choose a license for {device}"

#. {product} will use it.
#. Nearby approval: choose a license. Arguments: {product} = the product's name from ProductIdentity (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.chooseLede"
msgstr "{product} will use it."

#. This license is on all its devices. Remove one to make room for {device}.
#. Nearby approval: the license is on all its devices. Body under the Device limit reached title; the action opens the device list. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.deviceLimitBody"
msgstr "This license is on all its devices. Remove one to make room for {device}."

#. Wait a moment, then try again on {device}.
#. Nearby approval: too many attempts. Body under the Too many attempts title; the action is Done, because the retry happens on the new device. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.rateLimitedBody"
msgstr "Wait a moment, then try again on {device}."

#. Start again on {device}.
#. Nearby approval: the code expired. Body under the Code expired title; the person starts again on the new device. Arguments: {device} = the new device's friendly name (never translated).
msgid "signin.nearby.expiredBody"
msgstr "Start again on {device}."

#. Add it in Polaris Locker
#. The key was refused and the person adds it to their account on the web (↗, opens the browser).
msgid "signin.key.addInLocker"
msgstr "Add it in Polaris Locker"

#. macos: Add It in Polaris Locker
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "signin.key.addInLocker"
msgstr "Add It in Polaris Locker"

#. Scan to add this key in Polaris Locker on your phone.
#. The key-refusal step on TV and console: caption of the QR that opens the add-key page.
